 * @route /users/{id}
 * @description Retrieve user data by ID
 * @param int $id User ID
 * @return \Illuminate\Http\JsonResponse
 */
```

### Security Considerations

Make sure to validate and sanitize the user ID input to prevent potential security vulnerabilities, such as SQL injection or IDOR (Insecure Direct Object Reference) attacks. You can use Laravel's built-in validation features to achieve this.

```php
public function show($id)
{
    $id = (int) $id;

    $user = User::find($id);

    // ...
}
```

This code casts the `$id` variable to an integer, which helps prevent potential SQL injection attacks.

